# Tips and Tricks for Spotting AI Fictions

Developing habits of skepticism and verification is the best way to prevent the spread of misinformation through AI fictions.

>#### **💬 Quick Reflection:** When have you encountered an AI response that didn’t seem quite right? What made you question it?

Use the guide below to identify common signs of AI fiction and strategies you can use to respond.

<div style="max-width:90%; margin:0 auto; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color:#2f2f2f;">

<div style="border:2px solid #000; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden;">

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;">
<div style="background:#FDF4F2; padding:12px; font-weight:700; font-size:20px; border-right:1px solid #ddd;">🚩 Red Flags to Watch For</div>
<div style="background:#F2FBF8; padding:12px; font-weight:700; font-size:20px;">🛠 What to Do Next</div>
</div>

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:8px; padding:10px;">

<div style="background:#F8F6F6; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Confident tone without evidence</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">The response sounds certain but lacks sources or explanations</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#FAFBFC; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Reprompt or ask for sources</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Ask follow-up questions like “Are you sure?” or request evidence</span>
</div>

<div style="background:#F8F6F6; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Vague or overly general information</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Statements avoid specifics or meaningful detail</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#FAFBFC; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Ask for specifics</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Prompt for examples, details, or clearer explanations</span>
</div>

<div style="background:#F8F6F6; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Inconsistencies or contradictions</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Ideas don’t logically fit together</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#FAFBFC; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Cross-check information</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Compare multiple sources before accepting something as true</span>
</div>

<div style="background:#F8F6F6; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Fabricated details</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Quotes, citations, or facts that cannot be verified</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#FAFBFC; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Use a variety of tools</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Combine AI with search engines to verify facts</span>
</div>

<div style="background:#F8F6F6; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Answers that seem “too perfect”</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Well-written but overly simplified responses</span>
</div>
<div style="background:#FAFBFC; border-radius:10px; padding:8px; min-height:80px;">
<strong style="font-size:17px;">Exercise healthy skepticism</strong><br>
<span style="color:#555; font-size:15px;">Question information, especially for unfamiliar topics</span>
</div>

</div>
</div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
